{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Investigated and remediated the oversized tickets-branch history during an operator-authorized quiet window. Rewrote and published the authoritative store, then selectively transplanted exactly 21 authenticated audit-value events (CREATE=5, REVIEW_RESULT=7, LINK=9; 135,951 bytes; manifest SHA-256 eee3b2c6e1fb7a9c1df690ce4aa711ebfcc945c33b71223718a70ae82934dcf5) in publication commit 3239a5d7cb8c56f9b1ca940ecd4f8ab9da350f2a. Verified exact paths and hashes, reducers and links, and strict fsck from a fresh clone. Confirmed that none of the 1,520 removed comment aliases or 67 excluded enrichment events were restored, and that all six Jira duplicates remain absent while all six survivor records remain present. Preserved forensic AWS clones. Released the local quiet-window lock, re-enabled the Reconcile Bridge workflow, confirmed the AWS review bot healthy with HTTP 200, and resumed surviving paused processes. Closed nice-ashamed-crustacean and synonymous-senatorial-cuscus with signed PASS attestations. No code commit or Gerrit change was created. Known forensic caveat: the adopted AWS clone retains stale pre-rewrite reflog references; reachable remote history and fresh-clone fsck are healthy, and reflogs were intentionally not expired to preserve evidence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787846470259986001,"uuid":"38ac242b-82c9-4361-94d8-1648e6a83b09"}